At ordinary room temperature (\(T\approx298\ \text{K}\)) and atmospheric pressure, the molecular number density is

\[
n=\frac{P}{kT}
=\frac{1.013\times10^5}{(1.381\times10^{-23})(298)}
\approx2.46\times10^{25}\ \text{m}^{-3}
=2.46\times10^{19}\ \text{cm}^{-3}.
\]

Thus, \(1\ \text{cm}^3\) contains about \(2.5\times10^{19}\) molecules. Estimating the average separation as the cube root of the volume per molecule,

\[
d\approx n^{-1/3}
=\left(2.46\times10^{19}\right)^{-1/3}
\approx3.4\times10^{-7}\ \text{cm}.
\]

These values match **choice F**. Response A instead assumes \(0^\circ\text{C}\) and selects H, whose stated separation also differs from its own calculated \(3.3\times10^{-7}\ \text{cm}\). Therefore, Response A’s final answer is wrong and the gold answer is correct.

